$tests = @('The Area Code Masterpiece','The Bridge Connection','The City in Engraving','ZIP Code Color Statement','Two Shadows','The Navy Anchor','The Battlefield Cross','The Airport Hug','The Samurai Cat','The Airplane Pilot')
"== 10 TEST CARDS THROUGH THE REAL BATCH ROAD (REDO) - liked ones stay, the big draw skips them =="
foreach ($t in $tests) { $r = (RUN ("REDO " + $t) | Out-String); if ($r -match '->  (https://[^"]+)"') { "  " + $t + " -> " + $matches[1] } else { "  " + $t + " -> NOT DRAWN: " + ($r.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(220, $r.Length))) } }
"== NEW SERVICE & SACRIFICE BANNER =="
$subject = @'
A wide panoramic header banner for the "Service & Sacrifice" category of a tattoo website. On the right, a close-up real photograph, framed close from the waist up so both people fill the full height of the photo and both tattoos are large, sharp and easy to read: a strong man in his thirties with a short beard in a black tank top and a woman in her thirties with her hair pulled back in an olive tank top stand side by side in warm late-afternoon light, both flexing an arm toward the camera and showing their tattoos. His upper arm carries a bold, hard-hitting black-and-grey military tattoo of a soldier walking in full gear with a waving flag and a bald eagle above. Her upper arm carries a softer fine-line tattoo of a compass with a small dove and a delicate flag ribbon. On the left, on a deep charcoal background with warm gold light, the words "Service & Sacrifice" written large in strong engraved serif lettering in antique gold, surrounded by tattoo art of service - an anchor, a pair of boots, a dove rising, dog tags, a lighthouse and two soldiers walking side by side. The art fades softly into the photo through warm light and drifting dust. Proud, powerful and warm, high detail. Only the words "Service & Sacrifice", no other text, no watermark, no logos.
'@
$body = @{ subject=$subject.Trim(); model="gpt-image-2"; width=2048; height=768; exact_size=$true; raw=$true } | ConvertTo-Json -Compress
$j = (RUN ("SHOW_IT " + $body)) | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($j.payload.ok -and $j.payload.id) { "  BANNER Service & Sacrifice -> " + $j.payload.image_url } else { "  BANNER NOT DRAWN: " + $j.payload.error }
